<title>FRANCE: South Koreans take five pct in Oman gas group.</title>
<headline>South Koreans take five pct in Oman gas group.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>French oil group Total said that a South Korean consortium was taking a five percent stake in OMAN LNG, an operating venture for a $6.0 billion project to export Liquified Natural Gas from Oman from early 2000.</p>
<p>The South Korean Gas Corporation (KOGAS) comprises Yukong, Hyundai, Daewoo and Samsung.</p>
<p>Oman on October 23 signed a 25-year gas supply deal with South Korea's state utility Korea Gas Corporation.</p>
<p>With the South Korean participation the stakes of other investors will change.</p>
<p>Total will have 5.54 percent, the Omani government 51 percent, Royal Dutch/Shell 30 percent, Partex two percent, Mitsubishi 2.77 percent, Mitsui and Co also 2.77 percent and ITOCHU Corp 0.92 percent.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
